# The roots every confined session has beside its own: bin/lib/confine.py --session <file> lets
# a worker's or gate agent's commands remove and rename a directory entry only under a root, and
# each line here is one more, on every machine and for every task. A session's own roots are in
# its session file, which bin/lib/confine-session wrote at its launch.
# One path per line, absolute or starting with ~/ for the home directory the session file names,
# never the environment's HOME; a line naming nothing
# on a machine is skipped there, and one naming a link or anything but a directory is refused.
# This file is a guarded path (bin/lib/guarded), so each change comes back to Daniel for the
# per-head word.
# No path of the team home, of another worktree or of ~/.config/agent-team may be a root:
# confine.py refuses to run a command while a line is, holds or is under the team home,
# ~/.config/agent-team or ~/.claude, as the session file names them.
# ~/.rustup is no root: a worker installs no toolchain, and a confined launch's settings set
# RUSTUP_AUTO_INSTALL=0, so a missing one fails instead of downloading.

# The team's machine state, which scripts a worker runs write by rename: team-capacity,
# team-stack, and the library's lease probe cache.
~/.local/state/agent-team
# Cargo's own directory: cargo renames and removes entries under registry/ and git/ when it
# fetches or unpacks a crate, and takes ~/.cargo/.package-cache as its lock.
~/.cargo
# The sccache cache: the sccache server, which a session's first compile starts, writes and
# evicts cache entries by rename and removal.
~/.cache/sccache
